  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Dancing in the Street** (1 review): Playing is especially strong from the Dancing in the Street jam through the end of Deal [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Maggies Farm**: back after 230 archived shows (2873 days); mythic rare: 2 archived performances [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2024-05-25.Rainbowtoez.Shell** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 189 min; rated 1.67/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Best audio of the six tour shows taped so far: clear and loud in a pleasing way; Recording has good balance between vocals and instruments, which the room made difficult; reviewer suggests noting pull location in the data; Casey Jones appears twice in the upload, replacing Space, so Space is missing from the files [2][3][5]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: Crowd / 1st Set [1]\n- Audience chatter during the band's playing is audible and annoying on the recording [6]\n- Crowd noise swells in response to the Sphere's visuals rather than the music, which the recording doesn't capture [7]\n- A satellite passing overhead is audible as a zooming doppler thump on the recording [7]\n- Lineup: Weir on rhythm guitar, Hart on percussion, Mayer on lead guitar, Burbridge on bass; second set uploaded later [1]\n- Band sounds tightest of this tour so far; first set was short, five songs, under an hour [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2024-05-25.Rainbowtoez.Shell**: taped by Rainbowtoez; transferred by Hunter S; source: Channel 1: Apogee ClipMic digital 2 > iPhone [1]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Fan art by Honateez: [Dead And Company Show Sphere Las Vegas May 2024 Fan Gifts Home Decor Poster Canvas - Honateez](https://honateez.com/product/dead-and-company-show-sphere-las-vegas-may-2024-fan-gifts-home-decor-poster-canvas/) [9]",
